/E (Over the days of the session, you will spend a lot of time debating ideas, building compromises, and pushing your thinking beyond what feels comfortable and that is a big part of what makes an EYP session special. Still, I hope you will also remember that this experience is not only about the final output, but about the people you meet, the perspectives you encounter, and the small moments of connection that happen in between the formal parts of the programme. Some of your most valuable learning will happen in those spaces!)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
189 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 102 0 R
/E (I want this session to be one where you feel encouraged to be bold, curious, and open. Ask the difficult questions; share the perspective that feels most personal to you; listen carefully to others, especially when their experiences are different from your own. The strength of EYP has always been that it brings together people who do not think exactly alike, and asks them to create something stronger than any one viewpoint alone. That is not always easy, but it is always worth it.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
