/E (The history of Verona stretches back more than two thousand years. Originally founded by ancient tribes before becoming an important Roman settlement, the city still preserves remarkable monuments from the Roman era. The most famous of these is the Verona Arena, a massive amphitheater built in the first century AD. Even today, the Arena remains a center of entertainment and culture, hosting internationally renowned opera performances and concerts beneath the open sky. Walking through Verona is like stepping through different periods of history, as medieval castles, Renaissance palaces, and Roman ruins stand side by side throughout the city.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
